From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 09:30:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Re-exec the first process with 4K pages in an
 installed layout.

pre_exec re-execs the first process only when running from a build tree.
In an installed layout (wine.app) the first process kept the host's 16K
pages while every process it started ran 4K, so winepath, wineboot and
a game's launcher each began with a different page size than the rest.

Return 1 from pre_exec when getpagesize() != 0x1000 on arm64 macOS, so
reexec_loader goes through preloader_exec, which checks the entitlement
before the 4K exec. The re-exec'd process has WINELOADERNOEXEC set and
sees 4K pages, so it never execs again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index 2cca8d9f..9ac84488 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -2050,6 +2050,10 @@ static int pre_exec(void)
     }
 #ifdef HAVE_WINE_PRELOADER
     return 1;
+#elif defined(__aarch64__)
+    /* the first process starts with the host's 16K pages: exec once with 4K (preloader_exec checks the entitlement
+     * first), so that every entry point, a game, wineboot or winepath, runs 4K like the processes it starts */
+    return getpagesize() != 0x1000;
 #else
     return 0;
 #endif
